{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The Sosh theme is the theme dedicated to the Sosh brand only.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["🧬 Theme version: 2.7.0"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the Sosh theme any Sosh product must use, and cannot be subclassed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It embeds also in its target the Sosh brand colors which are not shared nor exposed in lower level targets or outside any module not depending to it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In other words, this "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesSosh\/documentation\/OUDSThemesSosh\/SoshTheme","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is based on the abstract ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", uses all the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Orange Unified Design System"}]},{"type":"text","text":" kit and brings the Sosh brand colors and assets."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This theme embeds and registers the fonts for the Sosh theme, you just need to use the theme object as is."}]}],"style":"tip","name":"Tip","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Sosh theme does not embed colors for charts yet and is read only: it cannot be subclassed or derivated","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"text":"How to use the theme","level":2,"anchor":"How-to-use-the-theme","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesSosh\/documentation\/OUDSThemesSosh\/SoshTheme"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. To use the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesSosh\/documentation\/OUDSThemesSosh\/SoshTheme","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" without further modifications, you will have to use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSThemeableView"},{"text":" for your root view and give it an instance of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesSosh\/documentation\/OUDSThemesSosh\/SoshTheme"},{"text":". Keep in mind the themes are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift class objects"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and can be heavy, so you may use only as instance as singleton and not store any properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct YourApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            OUDSThemeableView(theme: SoshTheme()) {","                \/\/ Your root view","            }","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then, in your views, you can simply use the theme through an environment variable to get the tokens:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SomeView: View {","","    \/\/ Get OUDS environment variable for theme thanks to themeable view","    @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","    ","    var body: some View {","        ","        \/\/ Use the theme to retrieve the tokens","        \/\/ For spaces: theme.spaces","        \/\/ For sizes: theme.sizes","        \/\/ For borders: theme.borders","        \/\/ For elevations: theme.elevations","        \/\/ For opacities: theme.opacities","        \/\/ For colors: theme.colors","        \/\/ For button configuration: theme.button","        \/\/ For link configuration: theme.link","        \/\/ Etc.","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"How-to-tune-the-theme","text":"How to tune the theme"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You cannot tune the Sosh theme."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Typography","level":2,"anchor":"Typography","type":"